{
  "$comment": [
    "Packages whose verdict both validators must agree on.",
    "The `.cheers-extension` grammar is enforced twice — in TypeScript by",
    "frontend/src/features/chat/workbench/extensions/package.ts and in Rust by",
    "server/src/domain/workbench_extensions.rs — because a personal-scope package is",
    "never uploaded, so the client cannot delegate validation to the server. Two",
    "hand-written validators drift, and these cases are the drifts that were actually",
    "found, frozen so they cannot come back.",
    "Each case is zipped and validated by both `cargo test` and `vitest`. `global` and",
    "`personal` are the verdicts expected at each scope (Rust's `allow_code` is false for",
    "global, true for personal). A file value that is a string is written verbatim; an",
    "object is serialized as JSON; an object with `$repeat` is that unit repeated `$count`",
    "times.",
    "Container rules — how a ZIP entry's declared size relates to its deflate stream —",
    "are not expressible here and stay hand-mirrored in each parser; the two sides use",
    "different ZIP implementations (fflate vs the `zip` crate).",
    "One known difference is deliberately absent: `\"schemaVersion\": 1.0` parses to the",
    "number 1 in JavaScript and is rejected by serde as a float. JSON.parse erases the",
    "distinction, so no TypeScript check can see it. The client accepting a package the",
    "server refuses costs an error message at upload, nothing more."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "declarative-package",
      "why": "A package of pure data is installable at every scope.",
      "global": "accept",
      "personal": "accept",
      "files": {
        "manifest.json": {
          "schemaVersion": 1,
          "id": "example",
          "version": "1.0.0",
          "title": "Example",
          "contributes": {
            "scenes": [
              {
                "id": "main",
                "title": "Main",
                "definition": "scenes/main.json"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "scenes/main.json": {
          "items": [
            {
              "id": "notes",
              "title": "Notes",
              "file": "notes.md"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "package-carrying-renderer-code",
      "why": "Renderer code is what global scope refuses and personal scope allows.",
      "global": "reject",
      "personal": "accept",
      "files": {
        "manifest.json": {
          "schemaVersion": 1,
          "id": "example",
          "version": "1.0.0",
          "title": "Example",
          "contributes": {
            "renderers": [
              {
                "id": "chart",
                "title": "Chart",
                "entry": "renderers/chart.js"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "renderers/chart.js": "export function render() {}\n"
      }
    },
    {
